<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<meta name="color-scheme" content="light">
<title>GI Map Checklist | Human Anatomy</title>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Lora:wght@400;600;700&family=Plus+Jakarta+Sans:wght@300;400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>
  :root {
    --cream: #FAF8F4;
    --cream-dark: #F0EDE6;
    --navy: #1C2E4A;
    --navy-mid: #2D4A6B;
    --sage: #6B8F71;
    --sage-light: #E8F0E9;
    --terra: #B5673A;
    --terra-light: #FAF0EA;
    --gold: #C49A3C;
    --gold-light: #FBF5E6;
    --teal: #3A7D7B;
    --teal-light: #E6F4F3;
    --rose: #9B4E52;
    --rose-light: #FAEAEB;
    --slate: #5A6B7A;
    --slate-light: #EBF0F4;
    --check-color: #4A7C59;
    --check-phys: #2A6E7C;
    --border: #DDD8CE;
    --text: #2A2A2A;
    --text-light: #666;
    --radius: 10px;
    --shadow: 0 2px 12px rgba(28,46,74,0.08);
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  html { background: #FAF8F4 !important; color-scheme: light !important; }
  body { font-family: 'Plus Jakarta Sans', sans-serif; background: #FAF8F4 !important; color: #2A2A2A !important; min-height: 100vh; }

  .site-header {
    background: white; color: var(--navy);
    border-bottom: 1.5px solid var(--border);
    padding: 22px 40px 18px;
    display: flex; align-items: flex-end; justify-content: space-between; gap: 20px; flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .header-left h1 { font-family: 'Lora', serif; font-size: 1.55rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1.15; margin-bottom: 3px; color: var(--navy); }
  .header-left p { font-size: 0.76rem; color: var(--slate); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.04em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .header-badge { background: var(--terra); color: white; font-size: 0.73rem; font-weight: 700; padding: 4px 13px; border-radius: 20px; letter-spacing: 0.04em; white-space: nowrap; }

  .tab-bar { background: var(--navy-mid); display: flex; align-items: stretch; padding: 0 40px; }
  .tab-btn {
    padding: 13px 26px 11px;
    font-family: 'Plus Jakarta Sans', sans-serif; font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #7A9BB5; background: none; border: none; border-bottom: 3px solid transparent;
    cursor: pointer; transition: all 0.2s; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px;
  }
  .tab-btn:hover { color: #C8DAEA; }
  .tab-btn.active-anat { color: white; border-bottom-color: var(--sage); }
  .tab-btn.active-phys { color: white; border-bottom-color: var(--teal); }

  .progress-bar-wrap {
    background: var(--cream-dark); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 11px 40px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px;
  }
  .progress-label { color: var(--slate); font-size: 0.74rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; white-space: nowrap; min-width: 110px; }
  .progress-track { flex: 1; height: 7px; background: var(--border); border-radius: 4px; overflow: hidden; }
  .progress-fill { height: 100%; border-radius: 4px; transition: width 0.4s ease; width: 0%; }
  .progress-fill.anat-fill { background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--sage) 0%, #4A9E6E 100%); }
  .progress-fill.phys-fill { background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--teal) 0%, #2A9D9B 100%); }
  .progress-count { color: var(--navy); font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 700; min-width: 52px; text-align: right; }

  .rubric-strip { background: white; border-bottom: 1.5px solid var(--border); padding: 9px 40px; display: flex; gap: 7px; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; }
  .rubric-label { font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--slate); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; margin-right: 4px; }
  .rubric-pill { background: var(--cream-dark); border: 1.5px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; padding: 3px 10px; font-size: 0.71rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-light); display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 5px; transition: all 0.25s; }
  .rubric-pill .pts { color: var(--navy); font-weight: 700; }
  .rubric-pill.met { background: var(--sage-light); border-color: var(--sage); color: #3A6645; }
  .rubric-dot { width: 6px; height: 6px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--border); transition: background 0.25s; }
  .rubric-pill.met .rubric-dot { background: var(--sage); }

  .main { max-width: 960px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 26px 22px 60px; }
  .panel { display: none; }
  .panel.active { display: block; }

  .legend { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 7px; margin-bottom: 22px; align-items: center; }
  .legend-label { font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.07em; color: var(--text-light); margin-right: 4px; }
  .tag { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 4px; font-size: 0.68rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.04em; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 3px 8px; border-radius: 4px; white-space: nowrap; }
  .tag-anatomy { background: var(--slate-light); color: var(--slate); }
  .tag-histo { background: var(--teal-light); color: var(--teal); }
  .tag-cells { background: var(--sage-light); color: #3A6645; }
  .tag-secrete { background: var(--gold-light); color: #7A5E1A; }
  .tag-neural { background: var(--rose-light); color: var(--rose); }
  .tag-function { background: var(--terra-light); color: var(--terra); }

  .phys-chip { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; font-size: 0.65rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 2px 7px; border-radius: 4px; white-space: nowrap; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .chip-on { background: #E8F5E9; color: #2E6B3E; border: 1.5px solid #A5D6A7; }
  .chip-off { background: #FDE8E8; color: #7B2020; border: 1.5px solid #F5AAAA; }
  .chip-effect { background: var(--teal-light); color: #1A5958; border: 1.5px solid #A0CECE; }
  .chip-integrate { background: var(--gold-light); color: #7A5E1A; border: 1.5px solid #DEC97A; }

  .region-group { margin-bottom: 9px; border: 1.5px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); background: white; box-shadow: var(--shadow); overflow: hidden; }
  .region-header { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; padding: 14px 20px; cursor: pointer; user-select: none; background: white; transition: background 0.2s; gap: 12px; }
  .region-header:hover { background: var(--cream); }
  .region-header.open { background: var(--navy); color: white; }
  .region-header.open .region-name { color: white; }
  .region-header.open .region-tag-line { color: #A8BAC8; }
  .region-header.open .region-progress-text { color: #A8BAC8; }
  .region-header.open .toggle-icon { color: white; }

  .region-left { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 11px; flex: 1; min-width: 0; }
  .region-icon { width: 33px; height: 33px; border-radius: 8px; background: var(--sage-light); display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-size: 0.95rem; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .region-icon.phys-icon { background: var(--teal-light); }
  .region-header.open .region-icon { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.15); }
  .region-name { font-family: 'Lora', serif; font-size: 0.96rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy); line-height: 1.2; }
  .region-tag-line { font-size: 0.7rem; color: var(--text-light); margin-top: 1px; }
  .region-right { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .region-mini-bar { width: 54px; height: 5px; background: var(--border); border-radius: 3px; overflow: hidden; }
  .region-header.open .region-mini-bar { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.2); }
  .region-mini-fill { height: 100%; border-radius: 3px; width: 0%; transition: width 0.3s; }
  .region-mini-fill.anat-mini { background: var(--sage); }
  .region-mini-fill.phys-mini { background: var(--teal); }
  .region-header.open .region-mini-fill { opacity: 0.8; }
  .region-progress-text { font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-light); }
  .toggle-icon { font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--text-light); transition: transform 0.25s; }
  .region-header.open .toggle-icon { transform: rotate(180deg); }

  .region-body { display: none; border-top: 1.5px solid var(--border); }
  .region-body.open { display: block; }

  .cat-block { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--cream-dark); padding: 12px 20px 14px; }
  .cat-block:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .cat-title { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 7px; margin-bottom: 9px; flex-wrap: wrap; }

  .check-list { list-style: none; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 5px; }
  .check-item { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 9px; padding: 6px 9px; border-radius: 6px; cursor: pointer; transition: background 0.15s; }
  .check-item:hover { background: var(--cream); }
  .check-item.checked-anat { background: var(--sage-light); }
  .check-item.checked-anat .check-text { color: #2E6040; }
  .check-item.checked-anat .check-note { color: #4A7A58; }
  .check-item.checked-phys { background: var(--teal-light); }
  .check-item.checked-phys .check-text { color: #1A4F5A; }
  .check-item.checked-phys .check-note { color: #2A6E78; }

  .check-box { width: 18px; height: 18px; border: 2px solid var(--border); border-radius: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; margin-top: 1px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; transition: all 0.15s; background: white; font-size: 0.68rem; color: white; }
  .check-item.checked-anat .check-box { background: var(--check-color); border-color: var(--check-color); }
  .check-item.checked-phys .check-box { background: var(--check-phys); border-color: var(--check-phys); }

  .check-text-wrap { flex: 1; min-width: 0; }
  .check-text { font-size: 0.845rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--text); line-height: 1.35; }
  .check-note { font-size: 0.74rem; color: var(--text-light); margin-top: 2px; line-height: 1.35; font-style: italic; }

  /* PHYSIOLOGY FEEDBACK CARDS */
  .feedback-row { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0; padding: 10px 11px; border-radius: 7px; border: 1.5px solid var(--border); background: white; margin-bottom: 8px; cursor: pointer; transition: all 0.15s; }
  .feedback-row:hover { background: var(--cream); border-color: #C0BBB0; }
  .feedback-row.checked-phys { background: var(--teal-light); border-color: var(--teal); }
  .feedback-row.checked-phys .check-box { background: var(--check-phys); border-color: var(--check-phys); }
  .feedback-row.checked-phys .fb-title { color: #1A4F5A; }

  .fb-header { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 9px; }
  .fb-title { font-size: 0.87rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy); flex: 1; line-height: 1.3; }
  .fb-rows { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px; margin-top: 8px; padding-left: 27px; }
  .fb-line { font-size: 0.78rem; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--text); display: flex; gap: 7px; align-items: flex-start; }
  .fb-line span:last-child { flex: 1; }

  .phys-intro { background: var(--teal-light); border: 1.5px solid #A0CECE; border-radius: 8px; padding: 13px 17px; margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 0.81rem; color: #1A4F5A; line-height: 1.55; }
  .phys-intro strong { font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy); }

  .reminder-box { background: var(--gold-light); border: 1.5px solid #DEC97A; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin: 20px 0 0; font-size: 0.8rem; color: #6A4E10; line-height: 1.5; }
  .reminder-box strong { font-weight: 700; color: #5A3E08; }
  .reminder-phys { background: var(--teal-light); border-color: #A0CECE; color: #1A4F5A; }
  .reminder-phys strong { color: var(--navy); }

  .rubric-summary { background: var(--navy); color: white; border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 18px 24px; margin-top: 24px; }
  .rubric-summary h3 { font-family: 'Lora', serif; font-size: 0.82rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 11px; color: #A8BAC8; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; }
  .rubric-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(180px, 1fr)); gap: 8px; }
  .rubric-row { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.06); border-radius: 7px; padding: 9px 13px; }
  .rubric-row-name { font-size: 0.74rem; color: #A8BAC8; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 3px; }
  .rubric-row-pts { font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 700; color: white; }
  .rubric-row-pts span { font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 400; color: #6B8499; }

  /* INSTRUCTIONS BLOCK */
  .instr-wrap { background: white; border: 1.5px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); box-shadow: var(--shadow); margin-bottom: 24px; overflow: hidden; }
  .instr-header { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; padding: 14px 20px; cursor: pointer; background: var(--navy); user-select: none; gap: 12px; }
  .instr-header:hover { background: var(--navy-mid); }
  .instr-header-left { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; }
  .instr-icon { font-size: 1rem; }
  .instr-title { font-family: 'Lora', serif; font-size: 0.98rem; font-weight: 700; color: white; }
  .instr-toggle { font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 700; color: #A8BAC8; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; white-space: nowrap; }
  .instr-body { padding: 22px 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px; }
  .instr-section { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 9px; }
  .instr-section-title { font-family: 'Lora', serif; font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy); border-bottom: 2px solid var(--cream-dark); padding-bottom: 6px; }
  .instr-section p { font-size: 0.845rem; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--text); }
  .instr-section strong { font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy); }
  .instr-card-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(220px, 1fr)); gap: 12px; margin-top: 4px; }
  .instr-card { background: var(--cream); border: 1.5px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 13px 15px; }
  .instr-card-title { font-size: 0.83rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy); margin-bottom: 7px; }
  .instr-card p { font-size: 0.79rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text); }
  .instr-tips { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 7px; }
  .instr-tip { display: flex; gap: 9px; align-items: flex-start; font-size: 0.83rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text); }
  .tip-dot { color: var(--teal); font-size: 0.5rem; margin-top: 6px; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .instr-callout { background: var(--navy); color: white; border-radius: 8px; padding: 14px 18px; font-size: 0.83rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .instr-callout strong { color: #A8C8E8; font-weight: 700; }
  .instr-body.collapsed { display: none; }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .site-header, .tab-bar { padding-left: 18px; padding-right: 18px; }
    .progress-bar-wrap, .rubric-strip { padding: 10px 16px; }
    .main { padding: 18px 12px 50px; }
    .tab-btn { padding: 11px 13px 9px; font-size: 0.73rem; }
    .region-header { padding: 12px 14px; }
    .cat-block { padding: 11px 14px 12px; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<header class="site-header">
  <div class="header-left">
    <h1>GI Map Checklist</h1>
    <p>Human Anatomy | Human Physiology</p>
  </div>
  <div class="header-badge">50 pts | Single Page</div>
</header>

<div class="tab-bar">
  <button class="tab-btn active-anat" id="tabAnat" onclick="switchTab('anat')">&#9998; Anatomy</button>
  <button class="tab-btn" id="tabPhys" onclick="switchTab('phys')">&#9889; Physiology</button>
</div>

<div class="progress-bar-wrap">
  <div class="progress-label" id="progressLabel">Anatomy Progress</div>
  <div class="progress-track"><div class="progress-fill anat-fill" id="globalFill"></div></div>
  <div class="progress-count" id="globalCount">0 / 0</div>
</div>

<div class="rubric-strip" id="rubricStrip">
  <span class="rubric-label">Rubric</span>
  <div class="rubric-pill" id="rpAnat"><span class="rubric-dot"></span> Anatomy <span class="pts">10 pts</span></div>
  <div class="rubric-pill" id="rpHisto"><span class="rubric-dot"></span> Histology + Micro <span class="pts">10 pts</span></div>
  <div class="rubric-pill" id="rpNeural"><span class="rubric-dot"></span> Neural <span class="pts">5 pts</span></div>
  <div class="rubric-pill" id="rpFunc"><span class="rubric-dot"></span> Function <span class="pts">5 pts</span></div>
  <div class="rubric-pill" id="rpVisual"><span class="rubric-dot"></span> Visual + Effort <span class="pts">15 pts</span></div>
  <div class="rubric-pill" id="rpAccuracy"><span class="rubric-dot"></span> Accuracy <span class="pts">5 pts</span></div>
</div>

<main class="main">

  <!-- INSTRUCTIONS BLOCK -->
  <div class="instr-wrap" id="instrWrap">
    <div class="instr-header" onclick="toggleInstr()">
      <div class="instr-header-left">
        <span class="instr-icon">&#128196;</span>
        <span class="instr-title">How to Build Your GI Map -- Read This First</span>
      </div>
      <span class="instr-toggle" id="instrToggle">&#9660; Collapse</span>
    </div>
    <div class="instr-body" id="instrBody">

      <div class="instr-section">
        <div class="instr-section-title">&#127912; This is a Visual, Not a List</div>
        <p>Your GI Map is a single-page illustrated diagram -- not an outline, not a study guide written in bullet points, and not a paragraph essay. If your final product looks like a table or a numbered list, start over. The goal is a hand-drawn or digitally designed <strong>map</strong> that traces the digestive tract from mouth to anus with annotated structures, zoom-in boxes, and brief labels. Think of it as a page out of a medical atlas that you made yourself.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:8px;">You are <strong>not</strong> being graded on artistic ability. Stick figures, rough sketches, and imperfect circles are completely fine. What matters is that you drew something -- a real visual representation -- not that it looks beautiful.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="instr-section">
        <div class="instr-section-title">&#128247; What "Visual" Actually Means</div>
        <p>Every region of the GI tract should be <strong>drawn</strong> as a shape on the page -- even a simple oval or tube. From that shape, you pull out and annotate. Here are the three visual tools you should be using:</p>
        <div class="instr-card-row">
          <div class="instr-card">
            <div class="instr-card-title">&#128269; Zoom-In Boxes</div>
            <p>Draw a small box or circle that zooms in on a specific region. For example: draw the stomach shape, then draw a small magnified box off to the side showing the gastric gland with labeled parietal, chief, G, and D cells. Connect it to the main diagram with a line or bracket. This is how you show histology without cluttering your main diagram.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="instr-card">
            <div class="instr-card-title">&#9635; Cross-Sectional Boxes</div>
            <p>At least one region should include a small cross-section diagram showing the four histological layers -- mucosa, submucosa, muscularis externa, and serosa/adventitia -- as concentric rings or layered bands. The small intestine cross-section is a great choice: you can show villi pointing inward, label the layers, and mark where Meissner\'s and Auerbach\'s plexuses sit between the muscle layers.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="instr-card">
            <div class="instr-card-title">&#8594; Arrows and Brief Captions</div>
            <p>Every label on your map should be a short phrase of 1-5 words, connected by an arrow to the structure it describes. Captions can be slightly longer (one sentence max) but should be written as annotations, not prose. Example: "Parietal cell -- HCl + intrinsic factor" is a good caption. A paragraph explaining the parietal cell is not.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="instr-section">
        <div class="instr-section-title">&#9989; Use This Checklist the Right Way</div>
        <p>The checklist in this tool is organized by region and category -- anatomy, histology, cells, secretions, neural, and function. Work through each region <strong>on your actual map first</strong>, then come back and check off what you included. Do not write out every checklist item as text on your map -- that defeats the purpose. Each item on this list should correspond to a label, a zoom-in box, a symbol, or an arrow on your drawing.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:8px;">A good gut check: if you can fold your map and all the information is still readable as prose without the drawing, you have not made a map. You have made a document. Go back and draw.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="instr-section">
        <div class="instr-section-title">&#128161; Practical Layout Tips</div>
        <div class="instr-tips">
          <div class="instr-tip"><span class="tip-dot">&#9679;</span><span>Start by sketching the full GI tract as a flow from top to bottom or in a winding path -- mouth at the top, anus at the bottom. Leave margins and blank space around each organ for your annotations.</span></div>
          <div class="instr-tip"><span class="tip-dot">&#9679;</span><span>Place accessory organs (liver, gallbladder, pancreas, salivary glands) off to the side with arrows connecting their ducts to the correct GI region.</span></div>
          <div class="instr-tip"><span class="tip-dot">&#9679;</span><span>Use color to differentiate regions or categories -- for example, one color for histology labels, another for secretions, another for neural structures. A simple legend in the corner is enough.</span></div>
          <div class="instr-tip"><span class="tip-dot">&#9679;</span><span>Reserve at least one corner or side margin for your cross-section or zoom-in histology boxes. These do not need to be large -- a 2-inch box is sufficient if it is clearly labeled.</span></div>
          <div class="instr-tip"><span class="tip-dot">&#9679;</span><span>For neural integration, mark Meissner\'s and Auerbach\'s plexuses directly on your cross-section diagram between the correct muscle layers -- do not just list them as text. Show their location.</span></div>
          <div class="instr-tip"><span class="tip-dot">&#9679;</span><span>For the physiology panel (A&P course): feedback loops should be drawn as small circles or loops with arrows marked "+" (stimulates) and "-" (inhibits). A loop that is one inch in diameter and clearly labeled is more valuable than a paragraph of text.</span></div>
          <div class="instr-tip"><span class="tip-dot">&#9679;</span><span>Scan or photograph your finished map at high resolution before submitting. Make sure all labels are legible in the digital version.</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="instr-callout">
        <strong>Bottom line:</strong> The rubric rewards completeness and accuracy -- not beauty. A clean, clearly labeled sketch that includes all required structures, histological layers, cell types, and functional annotations will score well. A gorgeous digital illustration that is missing parietal cells or the myenteric plexus will not. Draw first. Label accurately. Keep text short.
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>

<!-- ============================= ANATOMY PANEL ============================= -->
<div class="panel active" id="panel-anat">
